  "limits": [
    "Static native declaration/factory/constructor/binding/format trace; no native execution, actual Yi dispatch, live GPU state or final visual parity.",
    "The first 28-byte declaration matches the recovered CPU quad/ray packet. Draw-specific selection of this declaration and of the separately inspected default shader remains unobserved.",
    "The official Apple header supplies public Metal ABI enum names/values. This does not identify the SDK or compiler used to build the native client.",
    "Normalized vertex bytes do not establish native color-space, blend, texture-sampler or output-target state.",
    "No game behavior or asset changes in this witness. Ray color/UV producers, authored size mapping and clocks remain separate work.",
    "Original missing historical LLVM archives are neither replaced nor certified.",
    "The accepted application remains at 3086 passing tests out of 3088, the same two baseline failures, seven browser cases, fifteen exact packet pixel cases and the accepted production pack."
  ],
  "diagnostics": [
    "An initial bounded dyld decoder rejected a valid ten-byte ULEB delta because the shift counter exceeded 64 after its final byte. The final decoder bounds decoded integers to 64 bits, permits at most ten bytes and applies unsigned 64-bit address wrapping; a synthetic backwards-address case and malformed integer cases are retained.",
    "The first import-name hypothesis at 0x102000888 was objc_alloc_init; the existing import guard rejected it. Reading the indirect symbol table identified objc_opt_new, which the final witness checks.",
    "Several initial instruction/constant scans included unrelated functions. The final particle declaration was identified by the four explicit stream bindings at offsets 0,12,16,24 with stride 28; unrelated candidates are not treated as semantic evidence."
  ],
